class vsRecord
    doc One line of a data file (label, then values, then an optional { block } of child lines), and its children.
    doc The layout is the engine's public VS_Record.h; the exe's constructor and Init set the same places.
    size 0x78
    field 0x0 m_label vsToken
        doc The word before the values: "Name" in Name "Bob".
    field 0x30 m_token vsArray<vsToken>
        doc The values after the label. GetToken(i) and GetTokenCount() read it.
        seen vsRecord::vsRecord()+0x1b
    field 0x48 m_childList vsArray<vsRecord*>
        doc The lines inside its { block }.
        seen vsRecord::vsRecord()+0x44
    field 0x60 m_lastChild vsRecord*
        doc The child added last, while parsing.
        seen vsRecord::vsRecord()+0x64
    field 0x68 m_inBlock bool
        doc While parsing: inside this record's { block }.
        seen vsRecord::ParseString(std::string)+0x4a
    field 0x69 m_hasLabel bool
        seen vsRecord::vsRecord()+0x60
    field 0x6a m_lineIsOpen bool
        doc While parsing: more values can still join this line (Init sets it).
        seen vsRecord::Init()+0x233
    field 0x6c m_streamModeChildCount int
        doc In stream mode, how many children follow in the file; GetChildCount() returns it instead of m_childList's count.
        seen mmoColorGradient::SetFromRecord(vsRecord*)+0x36
    field 0x70 m_streamMode bool
        doc Read from a binary stream one child at a time (LoadBinary_Stream), so m_childList stays empty.
